⛔ CORRECTION, measured 2026-08-15 after the paragraph above was written and
published: these two callers were NOT exposed. --emit writes its banner
through json.dumps, whose default ensure_ascii=True escapes U+26A1 to
\u26a1, so its output is pure ASCII (measured: 797 B, zero non-ASCII chars)
and cannot raise on any codepage. The codepage crash is real and replayed at
render_debt_guard.py:1563, but on --scan, which NO hook in this file runs. A
real defect was attached to the wrong callers. Cured at the SUBJECT anyway
(render_debt_guard.py self-pins its streams on the script path), which covers
--scan, hand runs, and any future wiring; and a pending ruling proposes
wiring --scan into /wake, which would have wired the crashing path into every
wake had it landed first. The unpinned-caller note stands as a fact about the
wiring; it no longer stands as a statement of exposure.

