declares and any alternation-matcher hook was undeclarable BY CONSTRUCTION. The second
instance arrived exactly as that note predicted: tools/custody/rm_guard_hook.py
(under a fleet ruling, matcher `Bash|PowerShell`) could be neither staged nor declared, surfaced
as the contract's only orphan, and was reported onward as "untracked and undeclared"
when it is in fact tracked at 64b0c4013 and declared at .claude/settings.json:58 -- a
grammar gap reported as a custody gap. The grammar now accepts alternation and rm_guard
is declared above. git_guard is left STAGED: it is correctly covered either way, and
re-classifying a working declaration is a change with no defect behind it.

